Reused SMS login code and algorithms
-----------------------------------
Ximalaya-Downloader-Next, by sld272 and its contributors
https://github.com/sld272/Ximalaya-Downloader-Next
Revision: 765bae5cc07aaffa41797de2d3a9c963f1deb3e9
License: AGPL-3.0-or-later

Sources adapted:
- src/xdl/adapters/apk/client.py: nonce, SMS send/verify and quick login
- src/xdl/adapters/apk/native_py.py: login SHA-1 signature and RSA encryption
- src/xdl/config/apk.py: login protocol constants
- src/xdl/frontends/web_static/app.js: GeeTest/SMS integration

The earlier standalone export was xmly/login.py; its implementation is now
adapted into lib/api/xmly_login.dart and lib/pages/geetest_dialog.dart.
The original Nano WebUI is not included. The 2026-11-03/04 export adaptations
used bounded temporary sessions and caller-owned validation/settlement;
the Flutter migration retains these protections. Old Python sources were
removed after cutover. Upstream author notices are retained, and no upstream
download backend is incorporated.

Network service operators must provide users the Corresponding Source of the
version they run, including their modifications, under AGPL section 13.
The host application is responsible for offering that source to its users.

